 We are trying to teach the model made-up names (like a project codename) so it can recall them when a question is worded differently. Ordinary facts already work (about 69 of 72); made-up two-word names do not: the usual method gets about 12 of 72, our
 best write method about 40, and the goal is 61. Training the same small part of the model reaches 70 of 72, so that part is big enough, but only with side effects. ASTRA, which writes every word of the answer at once, got 14 of 72 against 12 and did not
 fit its targets, so it is closed. The offline math lab could not predict real results well enough and was stopped. Now: a check of the math behind earlier writes (NEW-1) and the step-7 setup.
